@startuml kbuild_flow
!theme plain
title Kernel Build System (Kbuild) Flow

participant User
participant Make as "make M=$(PWD)"
participant Kbuild as "Kernel Build\nSystem"
participant Compiler as "gcc/clang"
participant Linker as "Linker"
participant Output as "Output\n(.ko/.o files)"

== Build Invocation ==
User -> Make: make (out-of-tree module)
Make -> Kbuild: M=/path/to/module
note right of Make
  make -C /lib/modules/$(uname -r)/build
  M=$(PWD) modules
end note

== Kbuild Processing ==
activate Kbuild

Kbuild -> Kbuild: Read kernel build\nconfiguration
Kbuild -> Kbuild: Read driver Makefile
note right of Kbuild
  Parse obj-m, obj-y, etc
  Resolve dependencies
  Check kernel headers
end note

Kbuild -> Kbuild: Generate build rules
Kbuild -> Kbuild: for each .c file:

loop For each source file
  Kbuild -> Compiler: Compile to .o
  Compiler -> Compiler: Preprocess (.c)
  Compiler -> Compiler: Compile to assembly
  Compiler -> Compiler: Assemble to .o
  Compiler --> Kbuild: return .o file
end

Kbuild -> Kbuild: Link object files
Kbuild -> Linker: Link .o files → .ko
Linker -> Linker: Symbol resolution
Linker -> Linker: Generate module info
Linker --> Output: my_driver.ko

Kbuild -> Output: Store with version
note right of Output
  /lib/modules/$(uname -r)/kernel/
  or current directory
end note

deactivate Kbuild

== Verification ==
User -> Output: Check .ko
Output --> User: Module object ready for\ninsmod/modprobe

note right of Kbuild
  Key variables:
  - obj-m = compile as module
  - obj-y = compile into kernel
  - ccflags-y = compiler flags
  - M=$(PWD) = out-of-tree marker

  Kernel build system handles:
  - Include paths
  - Compiler flags
  - Symbol exports
  - Version checking
end note

@enduml
